From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Peirce <zak@peirce.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: report when the last PS4 guest process exits

The PS4 Wine server runs inside the title process and cannot use its normal
idle shutdown to end Wine. When its idle timer fires after all guest processes
have exited, report that state to the title over the already-captured stderr
descriptor. The title can then reload itself into the game launcher.
---
 server/request.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index 44ff43012e..c12e8c98aa 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -1669,6 +1669,10 @@ static void close_socket_timeout( void *arg )
     master_timeout = NULL;
     flush_registry();
 #ifdef WINE_INPROCESS_SERVER
+    /* The host title cannot end with the server thread. Tell it Wine has no
+     * guest processes left so it can return to its own launcher. */
+    write( 2, "PW_PS5_NO_USER_PROCESSES\n", sizeof("PW_PS5_NO_USER_PROCESSES\n") - 1 );
     return;  /* exiting would end the process that hosts the server */
 #endif
     if (debug_level) fprintf( stderr, "wineserver: exiting (pid=%ld)\n", (long) getpid() );
